Concrete Changes to Request in the AC Comment
Change the Licensing section from the W3C Document License to the W3C Software and Document License (or, at a minimum, apply the W3C Software and Document License to non-normative documents, test suites, and code/examples, and explain why the Document License is required on normative text given the tightening from the ATAG CG charter).
Clarify the ASC–W3C Memorandum of Understanding and joint deliverables, stating whether the MOU is executed and publicly available and how joint work with Accessibility Standards Canada interacts with W3C's Patent Policy and deliverable licensing.
Add target dates for non-normative deliverables (such as use cases/requirements, primers, and test/evaluation materials) and clarify how milestone dates will be tracked rather than treating all dates merely as non-binding estimates.
Confirm staffing and chair capacity (0.09 FTE) against expected coordination with AG WG, Web & AI IG, horizontal review groups, and ASC, and note how editor/implementer participation will be recruited beyond the initial CG group.
Tighten the Scope vs. Out-of-Scope boundary regarding WCAG 3 alignment and AI/LLM authoring tools so the WG remains focused on authoring-tool UI and content-creation support without duplicating or drifting into WCAG content-accessibility criteria.


